From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: macbox <macbox@localhost>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 03:50:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/34] a coherent surface answers to what it
 costs

A window a compositor samples syncs whole each frame with no trap: met_by's flush, on a surface
whose image the reader cannot sample. The demotion only saw traps and frames, and below 32 fps
never fired. A ledger of what a surface spends against the copies it replaces decides now, per
sync, with its cause counted; time outs double as they were meant to, which clearing eager_until
had undone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
